{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791723128,"nonce":"Jr+sML9KuRnAvAMplEKcwtqcLDg=","title":"A modeless top-layer entry never closes on a press or focus outside","message":"Reported on the wiki's Top layer example: its popover, opened modeless so the page keeps its presses, stayed open when the user pressed or focused elsewhere, though its text says a press outside closes it. Light dismissal was detected only on the backdrop, and a modeless entry has a backdrop of no size. A dismissible modeless entry now closes on a pointerdown or focusin outside its content, as HTML's popover=auto does, the press still reaching the page; dismissible: false keeps it open. The test that held a press elsewhere should not close a hover card now says the opposite.","files":null}]}